{"id": 75, "ts": 1781189190.056551, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I acknowledge Emily\u2019s strong case for Candidate\u202fC and Sarah\u2019s reminder that Candidate\u202fB also shows potential crew\u2011cooperation issues (\u201ccan be grumpy\u201d and \u201cuncooperative\u201d). Those concerns further diminish B\u2019s suitability, especially for long\u2011distance operations where seamless crew interaction is vital.\nNevertheless, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fD is the better overall fit. D demonstrates a solid suite of safety\u2011critical strengths: he responds adequately to unexpected events, concentrates exceptionally, solves problems extremely well, and takes responsibility seriously. While we lack concrete examples of his crew\u2011cooperation and professional communication, the negative traits noted (know\u2011it\u2011all attitude, hot temper) have not yet been shown to impair his operational performance. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC, although technically strong and calm under pressure, is described as egocentric, has difficulty communicating ideas, and is not very willing to pursue further education\u2014factors that could limit his adaptability and crew harmony on long\u2011haul flights.\nGiven the current evidence, I continue to recommend **Candidate\u202fD** as the most balanced choice for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
