{"id": 82, "ts": 1781189280.277421, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s emphasis on Candidate\u202fD\u2019s strong operational traits\u2014responding to unexpected events, high concentration, excellent problem solving, and serious responsibility. However, the same lack of concrete evidence that James just confirmed also applies to D\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation and professional communication, both critical for long\u2011haul operations. Moreover, D is described as \u201carrogant\u201d with \u201crelatively weak leadership skills,\u201d which directly undermines the crew\u2011cooperation and leadership criteria we need.\nCandidate\u202fC, on the other hand, is 100\u202f% reliable, creates a positive atmosphere with his crew, makes correct decisions quickly, stays calm in crises, and demonstrates solid technical competence. While C is noted as egocentric and has communication challenges, the positive crew atmosphere and full reliability suggest he can still maintain the collaborative environment required for long\u2011distance flights. The concerns about his willingness to further education and egocentricity are less immediate safety risks than D\u2019s unproven crew interaction and weak leadership.\nGiven the current evidence, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC offers the most balanced fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
